From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ieee1905: ieee1905 skip slow wifi dm probes
Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>

ieee1905: keep uloop alive with a 4addr/MLD backhaul (skip slow mt76 DM probes)

Three related problems on an MT7996/mt76 mesh node once a 4addr backhaul STA is
associated and MLD affiliated APs (ap-mld-N) exist:

1) One-time registration: allocating a dynamic 4addr AP/VLAN (wds_sta, e.g.
   wlan1-1.sta1) or an MLD affiliated AP (ap-mld-1) as a 1905 interface probes it
   via mediainfo/assoclist, which is slow enough to block ieee1905d's single
   uloop thread. The cost is the hostapd control socket: get_4addr_parent walks
   every netdev of the phy with STA-FIRST/STA-NEXT, and get_ccfs0_ccfs1 adds a
   round trip per interface. Fixed by detecting the AP/VLAN and MLD affiliated
   AP by name and skipping the probe at alloc; the AF_PACKET socket created
   later is all we need for RX.

   CORRECTED 2026-08-01. This paragraph used to say the probe "issues an
   NL80211_CMD_GET_STATION dump that mt76 never terminates". That was never
   measured - it came from reading the code on 2026-07-11, about a different
   caller, and was copied into three patch comments where it read as fact for
   three weeks. It is wrong twice over: on firmware 202607 `iw dev <if> station
   dump` returns in 0 s on ap-mld-N, bsta-mld-N and ap-mld-N.staM alike, with
   nothing left in D state; and platform_wifi_get_mediainfo() issues no station
   dump at all, only GET_INTERFACE. Only assoclist dumps, and it cannot on an
   AP_VLAN - nlwifi_get_assoclist_band() returns -1 unless the mode is AP.

   The wedge itself is real and measured (2026-07-13, kernel-stack sampling of
   a live daemon with an 8 s ubus call in flight): do_select / pselect6 on every
   sample, "never blocks in netlink recvmsg (so NOT a slow mt76 probe)". The
   bypass stays; only its stated reason was wrong.

2) Periodic 5s data-model self-refresh (i1905_dm_refresh_self): it re-runs the
   synchronous per-interface WiFi probes unconditionally - assoclist (hostapd
   wpactrl), per-neighbor GET_STATION link metrics, and mediainfo GET_INTERFACE -
   each 35-700ms on mt76. With the 4addr backhaul the neighbor set explodes, so a
   single refresh pass never completes (0 epoll for >20s): the uloop starves,
   every ieee1905 ubus call times out and 1905 TX stops, so the agent can never
   onboard (num_nodes stuck at 1).

3) On-demand ubus 'info'/'topology' path: i1905_dump_info() (the handler behind
   `ubus call ieee1905 info`, the CLI 'info' command, and the topology sub-table)
   calls platform_wifi_get_4addr_parent() for EVERY local interface. That is a
   blocking hostapd_cli/wpa_ctrl round-trip (wpa_ctrl waits in select() on the
   hostapd control socket - hence the daemon samples in do_select, not netlink).
   With the 4addr AP/VLAN and MLD affiliated APs present it stalls the handler
   inside the uloop, so `ieee1905 info` times out and mapcontroller never gets its
   AL-MAC. Gate get_4addr_parent behind skip_wifi_probe (managed interfaces) and
   IS_MEDIA_WIFI (unmanaged local interfaces): parent_ifname is only meaningful
   for the very 4addr wds_sta interfaces we already skip, so report "" for them.

These probes are not needed for onboarding or topology (which come from 1905
CMDUs) and the per-interface RX socket is independent of them. Add a cached
per-interface flag skip_wifi_probe (set for all WiFi interfaces at alloc) and
honor it in the refresh path and the on-demand info path. Ethernet interfaces are
unaffected (flag stays false).
--- a/src/i1905_dm.h
+++ b/src/i1905_dm.h
@@ -252,6 +252,7 @@
 	bool lo;			/** for cmdu loopback to localhost */
 	bool invalid;
 	bool is_brif;			/**< whether a bridged (slave) interface */
+	bool skip_wifi_probe;		/**< skip slow mt76 DM probes (uloop starvation) */
 	uint32_t brport;		/**< bridge port number when is_brif = true */
 	uint32_t br_ifindex;		/**< bridge (master) interface index when is_brif = true */
 	int nomaster;			/**< is set to 1 when not enslaved */
--- a/src/i1905.c
+++ b/src/i1905.c
@@ -357,6 +357,23 @@
 
 		info("%s: is WiFi\n", ifname);
 		n->mediatype = IF_MEDIA_WIFI;
+		n->skip_wifi_probe = true;
+		/* Dynamic 4addr AP/VLAN (wds_sta) "<ap>.staN" (e.g. wlan1-1.sta1),
+		 * and MLD affiliated APs "ap-mld-N": probing mediainfo/assoclist
+		 * here is slow enough to wedge ieee1905d's single uloop thread, and
+		 * even detecting it via platform_wifi_get_4addr_parent() blocks
+		 * (hostapd_cli). Detect by name (no syscall); the AF_PACKET socket
+		 * created later is all we need to RX their 1905 CMDUs. */
+		if (strstr(ifname, ".sta") || !strncmp(ifname, "ap-mld", 6)) {
+			info("%s: 4addr/MLD affiliated - skip wifi probe\n", ifname);
+			n->media = I1905_MEDIA_UNKNOWN;
+			n->num_mediainfo = 0;
+			n->mediainfo = NULL;
+			n->authenticated = true;
+			n->pbc_supported = false;
+			n->pbc_ongoing = false;
+			goto done;
+		}
 		ret = platform_wifi_get_mediainfo(ifname, &i1905_media,
 						  &n->num_mediainfo,
 						  (void **)&n->mediainfo);
--- a/src/i1905_al.c
+++ b/src/i1905_al.c
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@
 			int res = -1;
 
 			memset(&metric, 0, sizeof(struct i1905_metric));
-			if (wifi->role == IEEE80211_ROLE_AP) {
+			if (wifi->role == IEEE80211_ROLE_AP && !iface->skip_wifi_probe) {
 				res = platform_wifi_get_assoc_sta_metric(iface->ifname, nif->r_macaddr, &metric);
 			} else if (wifi->role == IEEE80211_ROLE_STA) {
 				res = platform_wifi_get_interface_metric(iface->ifname, &metric);
@@ -172,6 +172,9 @@
 		return 0;
 
 	/* get associated STAs */
+	if (iface->skip_wifi_probe)
+		return 0;
+
 	platform_wifi_get_assoclist(iface->ifname, stas, &numb);
 
 	/* get neigh entries reachable through this interface */
@@ -324,6 +327,7 @@
 	i1905_dbg(LOG_DM, "Updating mediainfo for '%s'\n", iface->ifname);
 	if_getmediatype(iface->ifname, &mtype);
 	if (mtype == IF_MEDIA_WIFI) {
+		if (!iface->skip_wifi_probe)
 		if (iface->mediainfo) {
 			free(iface->mediainfo);
 			iface->mediainfo = NULL;
@@ -332,6 +336,7 @@
 		}
 
 		iface->mediatype = IF_MEDIA_WIFI;
+		if (!iface->skip_wifi_probe)
 		platform_wifi_get_mediainfo(iface->ifname,
 						  &iface->media,
 						  &iface->num_mediainfo,
--- a/src/i1905_cmdresp.c
+++ b/src/i1905_cmdresp.c
@@ -317,7 +317,8 @@
 
 		aaa = blobmsg_open_table(bb, "");
 		blobmsg_add_string(bb, "ifname", iface->ifname);
-		if (!platform_wifi_get_4addr_parent(iface->ifname, parent))
+		if (!iface->skip_wifi_probe &&
+		    !platform_wifi_get_4addr_parent(iface->ifname, parent))
 			blobmsg_add_string(bb, "parent_ifname", parent);
 		else
 			blobmsg_add_string(bb, "parent_ifname", "");
@@ -499,7 +500,8 @@
 
 		aaa = blobmsg_open_table(bb, "");
 		blobmsg_add_string(bb, "ifname", ifl->ifname);
-		if (!platform_wifi_get_4addr_parent(ifl->ifname, parent))
+		if (!IS_MEDIA_WIFI(ifl->mediatype) &&
+		    !platform_wifi_get_4addr_parent(ifl->ifname, parent))
 			blobmsg_add_string(bb, "parent_ifname", parent);
 		else
 			blobmsg_add_string(bb, "parent_ifname", "");
